  "notes": "Magcubic HY300 Pro projector (rk3566_rgo, device adt3, Askey; Allwinner/HTC firmware), Android 11 (SDK 30)\nFirmware UI_Veng.projector.20260626.102242, 1280x720 panel.\nSame firmware family as the Portronics Beem 470 (examples/portronics-beem-470/), different build.\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<projector ip> tools/disable.sh examples/magcubic-hy300-pro/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<projector ip> tools/restore.sh examples/magcubic-hy300-pro/debloat.txt\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out anything you use.\n\nKept on purpose:\n- com.htc.htcsettings: the projector's own settings (Wi-Fi, picture, keystone). Home resolves to\ncom.htc.htclauncherhighenglishd08; it is left enabled, and the launcher takes Home with\n`cmd package set-home-activity`.\n- The firmware updaters (com.htc.htcotaupdate, com.softwinner.update, android.rockchip.update.service).\n- Factory and test packages (com.htc.hyk_test, com.softwinner.dragon*): not started, not disabled.\n- The input and source services: HDMI1-3 and CVBS1 list in the launcher's Inputs menu.\n\nThe Settings pill opens com.android.tv.settings; no settings_fallback_components entry is needed.\nApps nobody asked for",
